, "name": "All"}, "collaborativeOrgGroupCode": "*", "quantity": 20, "sequence": 14}, {"yearOfStudy": "*", "post": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "subject": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "subjectPost": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "typeOfProgram": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "designation": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "primaryOrg": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "associatedOrg": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "secondOrg": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "adminOrg": {"code": "*", "name": "All"}, "collaborativeOrgGroupCode": "*", "quantity": 20, "sequence": 15}], "linkedMeetingSections": null}], "duration": null, "cmCourseInfo": {"description": "This course examines the central place of cuisine and ecology to cultures around the world, with a focus on community growing, home cooking, food preservation, and experiences of gardens, restaurants, kitchens and marketplaces. Learning methods include oral interviews, field trips, sensory tasting and cooking sessions, multi-media experiential learning, as well as critical reading and writing.", "title": "Cuisine, Culture, Ecology", "levelOfInstruction": null, "prerequisitesText": "<p>9.5 credits</p>", "corequisitesText": "", "exclusionsText": "<p>GASD72H3</p>", "recommendedPreparation": "<p>FSTA01H3 or FSTA02H3 or FSTB01H3</p>", "note": "<p>Priority will be given to students enrolled in the Food Studies, Environmental Studies, and Environmental Sciences programs. Additional students will be admitted as space permits.</p>", "division": "University of Toronto Scarborough", "breadthRequirements": ["Social & Behavioural Sciences"], "distributionRequirements": null, "publicationSections": ["Food Studies"], "cmPublicationSections": [{"section": "Food Studies", "subSections": null}]}, "created": "2026-04-21@23:18:46.600", "modified": null, "lastSaved": 0, "primaryTeachMethod": "LEC", "faculty": {"code": "SCAR", "name": "University of Toronto Scarborough"}, "coSec": {"code": "", "name": null}, "department": {"code": "PESSC", "name": "Dept. of Physical & Environmental Sci (UTSC)"}, "title": null, "maxCredit": 0.5, "minCredit": 0.5, "breadths": [{"org": {"code": "SCAR", "name": "University of Toronto Scarborough"}, "breadthTypes": [{"kind": "BREADTH", "type": "Arts Lit & Lang", "description": "Arts, Literature & Language", "code": "Arts"}]}], "notes": [{"name": "Course Note", "type": "COURSE", "content": "<p><span><b>Field Course on Tasting &amp; Sharing Food Knowledge from Canada&rsquo;s Diverse Urban Worlds</b>. An experiential and outdoor learning course with limited enrolment (15), we gather, walk, talk, taste, &amp; explore the Greater Toronto Area (via public transit) from <b>May 4-13, 2026</b>. Highlights: Place-Based Edible Walks; Curated Museum Tour; Wild Foods Tasting; Indigenous Food Learning; Kitchen Sensory Experience; Culinary Master Class. Students request the course on ACORN. Status is INT (interim) until the instructor approves each student. Approved students are sent a link to to pay the ancillary fee <b>within 3 days</b> to complete the pre-enrolment requirement <i>(instructions how the ancillary fee to pay the department will be sent to approved students)</i>. Only after the fee is paid, are approved students are officially enrolled. Hence, no one is <b>officially enrolled</b>, until they pay the non-refundable <b>ancillary fee ($350)</b>&nbsp;within the 3 day period after they receive the notice of approval. If they do not pay the fee, they will be removed from the INT list, and the spot given to the next students on the waitlist. (The fee is non-refundable as food vendors &amp; visiting chef-professors require advance deposits to reserve time and supplies.)</span></p>\n<p><span><i>In-person field sessions + coursework: <b>May 4-13</b>: Compulsory workshops, 10-4 pm: Mon 4 May (SS2098, UTSG) &amp; Wed 13 May (SW313, UTSC); Optional fieldtrips (students will sign up for any 3 out of 4): Tue 5 May (10-4 pm) OR Wed 6 May (10-4 pm) OR Fri 8 May (5-9 pm) OR Sun 10 May (10-4 pm); Venues TBA.</i></span></p>\n<p><span><i>Coursework: &lsquo;Photovoice&rsquo; and &lsquo;Urban Food Story Media&rsquo; field-based assignments submitted in person, and electronically; no exams.</i></span></p>\n<p><span><i>Equipment: Presto card; re-fillable water-bottle; walking shoes; notebook/pen/pencils; loose lined paper; camera.</i></span></p>"}], "cancelInd": "", "subscriptionTtb": false, "subscriptionOpenData": false, "tb1Active": false, "tb2Active": false, "fullyOnline": false, "primaryFull": false, "primaryWaitlistable": false}]}